{"id": "thm-simplicial-and-singular-homology-agree-for-simplicial-complexes", "decision": "repair", "evidence": "Qualified the chain-map clause by a supplied global vertex order while preserving the canonical natural homology isomorphism without choice. Finite simplicial good-pair quotient excision is now proved by the barycentric open-star retraction, with relative simplex groups computed independently; a canonical finite-support argument selects all finite-order lexicographic minima and proves compact images lie in finite subcomplexes. Coning chain homotopies establish order independence and naturality. The original Statement change and full direct/indirect closure are recorded in agent-09-impact.json.", "sources_actually_read": ["items/cor-homology-of-good-pairs-is-reduced-homology-of-the-quotient.md", "items/thm-barycentric-subdivision-realizes-homeomorphically.md", "items/thm-compact-subset-of-a-hausdorff-space-is-closed.md", "items/thm-heine-borel-rn.md", "items/thm-extreme-value-metric.md", "Allen Hatcher, Algebraic Topology, Example 2.23 and Theorem 2.27, pp. 125, 128–130, https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/ATch2.pdf"], "files_changed": ["items/thm-simplicial-and-singular-homology-agree-for-simplicial-complexes.md"], "before_sha256": "bf04830f4a7c4ab7fc2f0b1581677a384b052b821db78ba2eaa83c933a88aee2", "current_sha256": "ead1a1821430b8a4c315dba8b7bb0a45a7a01dd97e5f354dc9819ca35703e29c", "statement_changed": true, "before_statement_sha256": "087e9cb0f462ce32ac64931b6d133e51094c347498f077c789f9d302dafee776", "current_statement_sha256": "51123cb1b27db18a351a15282d52c453bcd53a2cea916c485c9c180a42ab7011", "impact_file": "research/ap-131-sol-repair/agent-09-impact.json", "unresolved": [], "checks": {"precheck": "pass (focused two-item final run)", "rendercheck": "pass (focused two-item final run)", "diffcheck": "pass (focused two-item final run)", "independent_judge": "not_run"}}
{"id": "lem-ku-representability-and-skeletal-postnikov-d-three-comparison", "decision": "repair", "evidence": "Removed an unverified comparison theorem citation and supplied the actual argument: represent KU by the Bott Ω-prespectrum, translate the coefficient row into connective range, use the total-degree space ku_{p+q}, and identify the first cell-extension obstruction with the exact-couple d3. Handles negative representing-space indices, indeterminacy, p=1, and finite pairs. Second-reader recheck added Adams p. 391 Bott cofiber sequence, whose iterates identify the relevant p-connective cover of ku_{p+q} with ku_p, and expanded the skeletal attaching-cell connecting map that realizes d3; see agent-09-second-reader-review.md. Independent agent-05 follow-up identified and I corrected the A=empty cofiber convention: X_+ rather than X/empty; Statement unchanged.", "sources_actually_read": ["items/thm-cohomological-atiyah-hirzebruch-spectral-sequence.md", "items/thm-obstruction-theory-for-lifting-through-a-fibration.md", "items/lem-first-connective-complex-k-theory-postnikov-invariant-is-integral-sq-three.md", "J. F. Adams, Stable Homotopy and Generalised Homology, printed pp. 174–177, 245–247, 391–393, https://www.sas.rochester.edu/mth/sites/doug-ravenel/otherpapers/Adams-SHGH-latex2.pdf", "J. P. May, A Concise Course in Algebraic Topology, printed pp. 175–179, 204–208, https://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/CONCISE/ConciseRevised.pdf", "J. F. Adams, Stable Homotopy and Generalised Homology, Chapter 7, printed pp. 257–260, and Proposition 16.6, printed p. 391, https://www.sas.rochester.edu/mth/sites/doug-ravenel/otherpapers/Adams-SHGH-latex2.pdf"], "files_changed": ["items/lem-ku-representability-and-skeletal-postnikov-d-three-comparison.md"], "before_sha256": "73e05ddc050bf8fb973e6ab03371b756726a91200f134480464ff9c603e4ac01", "current_sha256": "86bace0b7583d139e2ac54e6a578dcd48aac621e86c47b15e51ad365450494f0", "statement_changed": false, "before_statement_sha256": "5fc