{"id": "thm-relative-homology-of-consecutive-cw-skeleta", "decision": "repair", "outside_maintenance": true, "evidence": "Removed the later general CW quotient supplier by explicitly proving the good-pair hypothesis for consecutive skeleta: an outer-annulus neighborhood retracts radially onto the lower skeleton, and transposition through C(I,V) with the CW weak topology proves product continuity for arbitrary cell sets and nonregular attachments. The earlier good-pair quotient corollary then identifies relative homology with the wedge of spheres. A second collar handles finite subwedges; the choice-free compact-image supplier passes cycles and boundaries to the arbitrary wedge. Degree zero and the no-cell case are handled separately. Statement unchanged.", "sources_actually_read": ["items/cor-homology-of-good-pairs-is-reduced-homology-of-the-quotient.md", "items/lem-compact-cw-images-have-finite-cell-support-without-choice.md", "items/thm-the-exponential-law.md", "items/lem-vanishing-relative-homotopy-extends-a-homotopy-inverse-over-successive-cells.md", "Allen Hatcher, Algebraic Topology, Section 2.2, https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/AT.pdf"], "files_changed": ["items/thm-relative-homology-of-consecutive-cw-skeleta.md"], "before_sha256": "8e123d8c15991be4fafe85a870890817cf04c13474fb0d24027979117805f123", "current_sha256": "9847287436a2070d1b6e6e400f95ffbaabbf4a12714f215260ae18d09fd53fc2", "statement_changed": false, "before_statement_sha256": "a252e2a4d1005d50c83b7ae6f6af680cf067d6689bed6212864e0d6f19259dc7", "current_statement_sha256": "a252e2a4d1005d50c83b7ae6f6af680cf067d6689bed6212864e0d6f19259dc7", "impact_file": null, "unresolved": [], "checks": {"precheck": "pass (focused two-item final run)", "rendercheck": "pass (focused two-item final run)", "diffcheck": "pass (focused two-item final run)", "independent_judge": "not_run"}, "before_snapshot": "research/ap-131-sol-repair/before/agent-09-thm-relative-homology-of-consecutive-cw-skeleta.md"}
